{
  "title": "Changing What's in a Box",
  "subtitle": "Variable Reassignment & Flow",
  "topic": "2.3 • VARIABLE REASSIGNMENT",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      2.3 • State Changes Over Time\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Changing What's in a <hlt>Box</hlt>\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 620px;\">\n      Variables are not carved in stone. You can replace what is inside a variable at any moment during program execution.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"lesson-ref-card\">\n    <div class=\"lesson-ref-header\">\n      <span class=\"ref-badge\">PREVIOUS KNOWLEDGE</span>\n      <span class=\"lesson-ref-title\">Connecting to Earlier Concepts</span>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"lesson-ref-desc\">\n      In Chapter 2.3, we saw that Python executes statements line by line, strictly in order from top to bottom.\n    </p>\n    <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=2&sub=6&ref_from=1_3_7\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: Order of Execution (Lesson 2.3) →</a>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Analogy • Whiteboard, Not a Stone Tablet\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Erasing and Writing a New Value\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      Think of a variable as a label written on a whiteboard. You can write <hlt>25</hlt>, then erase the 25 and write <hlt>30</hlt> in its place. The label stays the same, but the value inside changes.\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      age = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">25</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(age)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Line 2 outputs: 25</span><br/>\n      age = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">30</span>    <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># The old value 25 is replaced with 30!</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(age)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Line 4 outputs: 30</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #a5f3fc; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 18px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Real-World Match • The Sports Scoreboard\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Labels Stay Constant, Scores Update\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      A scoreboard at a sports stadium starts at <hlt>score = 0</hlt>. Whenever a team scores points, the display is updated to <hlt>score = 50</hlt>. A variable only holds ONE value at any single moment.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}